        "original_id": "e5bdd3ae-95ed-5d37-8cf9-455a1ed12171",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lewis Sheridan Leary, Mary Patterson, Charles Henry Langston, Langston Hughes, John Brown\n- Places: Oberlin, Ohio, Harpers Ferry, Joplin, Missouri\n- Roles: harnessmaker, poet, social activist, novelist, playwright, columnist\n- Events: John Brown's raid on Harpers Ferry\n\nFacts:\n- Lewis Sheridan Leary was born on March 17, 1835.\n- Lewis Sheridan Leary was an African-American harnessmaker from Oberlin, Ohio.\n- Lewis Sheridan Leary joined John Brown's unsuccessful raid on Harpers Ferry.\n- Lewis Sheridan Leary was killed at Harpers Ferry on October 20, 1859.\n- Lewis Sheridan Leary was the first husband of Mary Patterson.\n- Mary Patterson later married Charles Henry Langston.\n- By her marriage to Charles Henry Langston, Mary Patterson became the maternal grandmother of Langston Hughes.\n- Langston Hughes, born James Mercer Langston Hughes on February 1, 1902, was an American poet, social activist, novelist, playwright, and columnist from Joplin, Missouri.\n- Langston Hughes died on May 22, 1967.",
